            "Packed BCD stores two decimal digits in a single 8-bit byte (used in x86 DAA/DAS instructions, real-time clock chips like DS1307, and financial/mainframe arithmetic), whereas unpacked BCD stores one digit in the lower 4 bits of each byte.",
