            "Legacy formats such as Apache APR1 ($apr1$, iterated salted MD5) and unsalted Base64 SHA-1 ({SHA}) exist strictly for older tooling or Windows Apache compatibility. Because unsalted {SHA} hashes can be reversed instantly with rainbow tables if the file leaks, prefer Bcrypt everywhere modern.",
