          question: "Why do proto3 int64 and uint64 fields default to JSON string instead of integer?",
          answer: "JavaScript and JSON parsers built on IEEE 754 64-bit floats lose precision above 9,007,199,254,740,991 (2^53 - 1). Google’s ProtoJSON encoding serializes 64-bit integers as decimal strings so IDs and timestamps stay exact.",
