          heading: "How the official Tailwind CSS class ordering hierarchy works",
          paragraphs: [
            "Tailwind CSS compiles utilities in stylesheet cascade order, so reading class strings in the same order they appear in Tailwind’s generated CSS makes conflicting overrides obvious at a glance. The official Prettier sorting order places base layout and positioning first (block, flex, grid, relative, z-10), followed by box sizing and spacing (m-*, p-*, w-*, h-*), typography (text-*, font-*), backgrounds and borders, visual effects, and transitions.",
            "Variant-prefixed classes (hover:, focus:, dark:, sm:, md:) are grouped after unprefixed base classes in mobile-first breakpoint order so responsive overrides remain easy to audit.",
          ],
